     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the FDA maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Most guidelines recommend 2,000 mg/day or less. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg or 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is a typical starting or titration dose.\n- **1,700 mg/day in total.** This could be split as 850 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note recording that it was intentional. I'd advise against that dose."
      }
     ],
